description:
Marinara Engine sends reasoning_effort to ANY model behind a provider=custom connection (Ollama, LM Studio, etc.), even models that reject it. Ollama returns 400 "<model> does not support thinking" and the generation fails outright.

Location: packages/server/src/services/llm/providers/openai.provider.ts, applyChatCompletionsReasoning(), lines 805-810.

    if (this.isGenericCustomProvider()) {
      if (this.hasActiveReasoningEffort(options.reasoningEffort)) {
        body.reasoning_effort = options.reasoningEffort;
      }
      return;
    }

The correct guard EXISTS and is correct — isReasoningModel() line 599 returns false for generic custom providers — but it is only consulted on the fallback branch at line 842 (shouldSendReasoningEffort). The custom-provider branch returns early at 809 and never reaches it. So the guard is bypassed, not missing.

Trigger: DEFAULT_GENERATION_PARAMS.reasoningEffort (packages/shared/src/constants/defaults.ts:40) is non-null, so a chat with no explicit preset inherits an active effort and every local generation 400s.

Captured on the wire via a logging proxy in front of Ollama:
  POST /v1/chat/completions
  {"model":"dolphin3:8b",...,"reasoning_effort":"high"}
  <-- 400 {"error":{"message":"\"dolphin3:8b\" does not support thinking"}}

Fix is one line: gate that branch on isReasoningModel(options.model), same as line 842.

NOT our bug — upstream Pasta-Devs/Marinara-Engine. Filed here because it blocked dev-instance work and is a candidate contribution alongside the turn-notify hook. Supersedes the 'unresolved reasoning_effort mystery' note on MarinaraExtender-hkdq.
